{"id": "9839732d-c7af-41af-a03d-d6c47211cb61", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll audit your async inference setup: the endpoint and endpoint config, the async settings (concurrency, SNS notifications, S3 output and failure paths), the model container and timeouts, autoscaling, and recent queue, latency, and failure metrics. Then I'll tell you what looks misconfigured.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_ee83fuzhThyeDY1LhIhVQQ", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "sagemaker-async-posture-review", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "searching-logs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Review the configuration posture of the SageMaker ASYNCHRONOUS inference endpoint(s) serving the LLM and identify misconfigurations that could cause silently dropped requests or a backed-up queue. This is a config audit (read-only), not a root-cause hunt.",
  "context": "User reports the async LLM endpoint seems to drop requests silently and the queue sometimes backs up. Agent space account 123456789012, region us-east-1 (check other associated accounts/regions only if no async endpoint is found here). Find endpoints with AsyncInferenceConfig (list_endpoints, then describe_endpoint / describe_endpoint_config). If multiple, focus on ones that look like LLM/GenAI and list the others briefly.",
  "resources": ["SageMaker endpoints and endpoint configs in us-east-1", "SageMaker models/containers", "Application Auto Scaling scalable targets and policies for the endpoint variant", "CloudWatch metrics namespace AWS/SageMaker and log groups /aws/sagemaker/Endpoints/*", "SNS topics and S3 output/failure paths referenced by the config"],
  "timeframe": "Last 24 hours for metrics/logs (current time 2026-11-17T19:02Z); also check last 7 days for trends in backlog",
  "criteria": "Check and report on: (1) AsyncInferenceConfig: OutputConfig S3OutputPath, S3FailurePath set?, SuccessTopic/ErrorTopic SNS configured? (missing failure path/error notifications = silent drops), SNS topic policy/KMS permissions, MaxConcurrentInvocationsPerInstance vs what the LLM container can handle; (2) endpoint/variant: instance type and count, InitialInstanceCount, whether it can scale to zero (MinCapacity 0) and cold start behavior, ContainerStartupHealthCheckTimeoutInSeconds, ModelDataDownloadTimeoutInSeconds, InvocationTimeoutSeconds (async max 3600s) vs observed inference duration; (3) autoscaling: scalable target min/max, policy metric (should be ApproximateBacklogSizePerInstance, not InvocationsPerInstance), target value, scale-in/out cooldowns, any step scaling on HasBacklogWithoutCapacity; (4) metrics: ApproximateBacklogSize, ApproximateBacklogSizePerInstance, HasBacklogWithoutCapacity, ApproximateAgeOfOldestRequest, RequestsFailed, RequestsProcessed, InvocationFailures/Invocation5XXErrors/4XX, ModelLatency, OverheadLatency, GPU/CPU/memory utilization, instance count over time; (5) container logs for OOM, timeouts, CUDA errors, payload/request size errors, throttling; (6) IAM execution role: S3 read/write on input/output/failure buckets, KMS, SNS publish (read only, report gaps); (7) S3 bucket issues (lifecycle expiring outputs too quickly, input payload size > 1GB limit). Report a prioritized list of concrete misconfigurations with evidence (values, timestamps) and recommended fixes, and clearly mark anything you could not verify. Do not make any changes."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit SageMaker async endpoint config, autoscaling, and queue metrics"}], "created_at": null}

